<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Legnano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1176">1176</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Legnano</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Legnano was fought in 1176 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> Frederick I Barbarossa. The defeat showed the limits of imperial military power, which depended on princely contingents that could not be sustained against organised civic resistance. It forced the emperor to accept a negotiated settlement with the Italian cities and is cited in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>'s military history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano.jpg" alt="Battle of Legnano" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Faberh at Italian Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BattagliaLegnano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
